WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.180
When Pixar began developing the third Cars
movie, they decided to return to the roots

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.960
of the franchise with a story centred firmly
around Lightning McQueen.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.200
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to explain all

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.400
the deleted scenes, original stories and alternate
endings that Pixar developed for Cars 3 during

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.650
five years of production but that didn't make
it into the final movie.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.939
Also I'm running my Cars 3 giveaway for two
The Art of Cars 3 hardback books on this video.

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:31.650
If you'd like a chance to win one of these
two very cool books which feature gorgeous

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:36.899
concept art and storyboards from Cars 3, be
sure to subscribe, leave a comment about the

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:40.460
film, and also answer the question I'll be
asking later in the video.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.120
Quick warning, I will be discussing spoilers
in this video, so take care if you haven't

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.370
seen the movie yet.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.570
After director John Lasseter made the first
Cars movie, he was really keen for legendary

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.489
actor Paul Newman to return as the voice of
Doc Hudson for the sequel.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:00.850
Sadly though, Newman passed away in 2008,
and while Cars 2 does make brief mention of

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.220
Doc, details of how Doc died were never revealed
in that movie.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.790
However, in an interview with Screencrush,
Cars creative director Jay Ward explained

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.979
that he had hoped to remedy the lack of details
about Doc's passing in Cars 3.

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:16.980
In fact, in an early version of the movie,
there was going to be a flashback that would

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.689
have revealed how Doc died.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.090
Ward described the deleted scene as "a really
tender moment where McQueen [is] driving and

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.670
Doc's following him and it's like the day
your mentor passes away."

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.660
Although Pixar loves to make us cry, the scene
was cut because, as Ward himself said, it

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.660
was "just depressing".

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.470
I still think that this could have been an
interesting scene to include as although many

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:41.650
Cars and Pixar fans enjoyed Cars 3, many still
want to know what really happened to Doc.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:47.290
And, as Pixar proved in their incredible introductory
montage of Carl and Ellie in Up, a character's

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:52.350
death can provide a deeper emotional connection
to a movie and its story.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:56.550
One of the best moments in the new movie is
when Lightning, Cruz and Mack go incognito

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.820
at the Thunder Hollow demolition derby.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.171
Lightning covers himself in mud and takes
on the name of Chester Whipplefilter, Cruz

00:02:03.171 --> 00:02:08.259
uses the alias Frances Beltline, and Mack
wears a Jocko Flocko disguise, which, if you've

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:13.070
watched my Cars 3 easter eggs video, you'll
know is a sneaky easter egg to a real-life

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.540
NASCAR monkey racer.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:20.240
But the theme of Team 95 operating and training
under cover was originally going to be a much

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.600
more extended and long-running joke throughout
the movie.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.580
For example, initially the beach training
scene was going to be set up as a pretend

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.640
movie shoot where Guido was an Italian film
director and Lightning was an actor pretending

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.080
to be Lightning McQueen.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.250
A bunch of other gags about the team travelling
around in disguise were also cut from the

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.980
final film, for example, Mack was going to
conceal his identity in various ways ranging

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:48.550
from a travelling circus to a shipping container,
and from a military vehicle to a lumberjack.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:53.360
The character of Cruz Ramirez was very different
in early drafts of the story and initially

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.920
she was actually a male car, but the filmmakers
decided to make her a female car so she was

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.190
more of an outsider in the typically male-dominated
world of motor racing.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.920
Originally, Cruz was also going to be a young
rookie racer rather than a trainer and an

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:11.080
early idea was that when Lightning met her
at the Rust-Eze Training Centre, he would

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.420
see her as a younger version of himself, in
a very similar way to how Doc viewed Lightning

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.070
when he first met him in the first movie.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:21.810
In the end though, the filmmakers felt this
was re-treading too much of the story from

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:26.450
Cars 1, so they began to make her more of
an opposite character to Lightning, for example

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.120
in the way she lacked confidence.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.500
Ultimately, the movie's creators believed
these changes to Cruz's character helped build

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.390
a more interesting story by developing a more
odd-couple-style of relationship between Lightning

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:39.240
and his new trainer.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:44.160
The relationship between Lightning and Cruz
culminates in the Florida 500 Piston Cup event

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.640
where, midway through the race, Lightning
realises that Cruz is the answer to beating

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.790
Jackson Storm, so he calls her back for his
pit stop but instead of going back out himself,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:58.300
he gives her his number 95 and tells her to
race in his place.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.130
Before settling on this final twist though,
the filmmakers considered a whole bunch of

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.810
alternate endings.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.130
In one of those alternatives, Lightning never
took part in the final race at all and entered

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.520
Cruz into the race instead, presenting her
as the "New 95" to his friends from Radiator

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.480
Springs before the event.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.160
This ending didn't work well because the filmmakers
found that there was a sense that the movie

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.370
was already finished at the point that Lightning
decided to stop racing which meant that the

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.160
remaining story felt underwhelming.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.850
In another ending, McQueen ran the whole race
himself, won it, and then he decided to mentor

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.540
Cruz only at the very end of the movie.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:37.400
However, this ending made the film "feel hollow",
according to director Brian Fee.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.290
In yet another version, they both took part
in the race and had to compete against each

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:45.510
other, but that didn't work either because
it split the audience over who to support.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.600
In the end, the filmmakers decided that, to
get the right level of tension in the movie's

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.870
final act, they would have Lightning pass
on his number mid-race to Cruz.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.460
But even then, there were further variations
considered within this scene.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.630
For example, at one point, this passing of
the torch to Cruz was going to be more fraught

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:05.730
with McQueen getting angry at her when she
didn't understand what was going on, though

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:09.810
finally they both would have come to a proper
understanding and appreciation of each other.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:14.470
I'm not sure quite how I feel about the way
the number 95 was passed to Cruz in the final

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:19.630
film, as although Smokey explained that "the
rules only say the number has to be out there,

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.850
doesn't say who has to wear it", the confusion
it initially created meant this transition

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.350
wasn't quite as smooth as I would have liked.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:30.510
The Cars 3 filmmakers obviously spent a lot
of time considering all the possible options,

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.270
but I still wonder whether there was another
way to have done this that didn't raise quite

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.120
so many questions in my mind while I was watching
it.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.700
What do you think about the ending?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.900
Did you enjoy it or would you have preferred
something different?

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:47.660
By the way, there are some interesting storyboards
which hint at a deleted scene or another alternate

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.680
ending where McQueen reveals his transformation
into the Fabulous Lightning McQueen at the

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.690
Piston Cup race rather than at the very end
of the movie.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.950
You can see him emerging with Doc's colours
and the number 51 to a group of press, then

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:03.480
the crowd and, finally, onto the racetrack
where he faces up to Jackson Storm.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:07.470
In the final movie, the reveal of the "Fabulous
Lightning McQueen" is a much more private

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.080
moment for Lightning with his friends at Radiator
Springs.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.070
Although the movie's final scene of Lightning
unveiling his homage to Doc Hudson was lovely,

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:19.460
these storyboards hint that the filmmakers
considered a much more dramatic and symbolic

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.520
way of 'bringing Doc back to life through
his protégé', to quote story supervisor

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.750
Scott Morse, by having Lightning announce
his new number and colours at the Piston Cup.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.170
I'm not sure if this would have fit the way
the rest of the ending played out, but perhaps

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:35.680
fans of Doc Hudson especially would have enjoyed
seeing this scene.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:42.020
Production on Cars 3 began at Pixar in 2013,
but it wasn't until 2015 that the final direction

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:46.590
of the story was decided on after John Lasseter
was inspired by the retirement of his friend,

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.150
professional NASCAR racer, Jeff Gordon at
the age of 43.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:54.460
Which means that, during those 2 years, various
fascinating ideas and stories were considered

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.460
for the sequel.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:07:01.210
Some of those early ideas involved returning
to Route 66 and also including Route 99 and

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.050
racing on dry bed lakes (insert pictures).

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:07.520
One idea that was developed in a little more
detail was an exploration of Southern California

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.040
car culture plus celebrity culture in LA.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:14.889
In an interview with ScreenJunkies News, director
Brian Fee revealed that in one early story

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:18.930
Lightning "went to a Hollywood Hills party
and it was full of actors, and we had the

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.700
old Batmobile and the new Batmobile talking
to each other at a party."

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:26.240
Obviously, this was a whole other story, but
I imagine this scene could have been a lot

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:31.139
of fun as we already saw car versions of Pixar
movie characters from Toy Story, Monsters

00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:35.180
University, and A Bug's Life in the credits
for the first Cars movie, and I imagine there

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:39.180
could have been a lot of potential for jokes
and voice cameos by previous Batman actors

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.180
or sound-alikes.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:45.070
I also wonder whether an LA-based story might
have explored Sally's past history in the

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.070
city.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:50.070
If you recall, in the first Cars movie, we
learned that Sally was originally a hot-shot

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:54.250
lawyer in Los Angeles, and it could have been
interesting to see her backstory explored.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:59.520
So, are there any deleted scenes or stories
you would love to have seen in Cars 3?

